.vs/
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
*.tmp
~$*

# .NET
src/**/bin/
src/**/obj/
*.user

# wwwroot/lib/ used to be gitignored ("fetched via libman") but no libman.json
# or restore step ever existed, so a fresh clone/worktree/publish silently had
# no Bootstrap/jQuery at all. Now tracked directly in Git instead — see the
# exact 9 files kept (5 used by _Layout.cshtml/_ValidationScriptsPartial.cshtml
# + 4 accompanying LICENSE files) in docs/LOCAL-STAGING.md.

# RazorSDK's scoped-CSS bundle — `dotnet publish` (but not `dotnet build`/`run`)
# copies this into wwwroot/ on its own; a generated, fingerprint-named build
# artifact, never source, in case it ever ends up here.
src/MVTeaches.Web/wwwroot/*.styles.css

# Local Staging runtime state (Data Protection keys, uploaded receipts) —
# persistent on purpose (outside bin/), but machine-local and never committed.
src/MVTeaches.Web/App_Data/

# Local Staging's own secrets (ConnectionStrings:MvTeaches, StagingSeed:*,
# Bootstrap:*) — loaded by Program.cs only when this file exists; never a
# machine-wide environment variable, never committed. See docs/LOCAL-STAGING.md.
src/MVTeaches.Web/appsettings.Staging.secrets.json

# The same mechanism, any variant of it. scripts/new-clean-trial-db.ps1 writes
# appsettings.CleanTrial.secrets.json, and a wildcard rather than one more
# literal line is deliberate: the next such file must be ignored the moment it
# is written, not the moment somebody remembers to add it here.
src/MVTeaches.Web/appsettings.*.secrets.json
